        "body": "The cancellation part was real: the loop kept calling `next()` after cancel as long as values were skipped and the iterator had no `return()` (generators already stop there). af78734 adds a `cancelled` flag that ends the loop, with a test that fails on the previous commit in both web and node.\n\nI left out the macrotask yield. An iterator that keeps returning skipped values without awaiting anything would spin a `for await` loop the same way, and `iterable()` doesn't schedule timers anywhere else, so I'd rather not add one for this case.",
